  "@id": "https://pices-data.github.io/odis/records/zenodo-23569233.jsonld",
  "@type": "Dataset",
  "name": "Oceanographic Data from the Eastern Bering Sea by the F/V Sea Storm during the Summer and Fall 2003",
  "description": "Oceanographic data were collected in the eastern Bering Sea by the U.S. F/V Sea Storm from August to October 2003. At stations over the eastern Bering Sea shelf, the F/V Sea Storm used a Sea-Bird SBE 19 Seacat profiler from surface to near bottom depths to measure temperature, salinity, chlorophyll a fluorescence, light transmission and photosynthetic available radiation (PAR), and along-transect surface temperature and salinity data were measured continuously with a thermosalinograph mounted aboard ship.\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: To collect oceanographic data as part of the BASIS survey of the Bering Sea.",
  "url": "https://zenodo.org/records/23569234",
